<title>ECUADOR: Latin coffee producers lash out at speculators.</title>
<headline>Latin coffee producers lash out at speculators.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delegates to a meeting of the CEV group of Latin American coffee producers lashed out at speculators and called for greater coordination between major exporters Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We depend on a market of speculation or on organizations which do not have anything to do with coffee,&quot; said Fernando Montes, director of the Honduras Coffee Institute.</p>
<p>He said that export quota programs should be stepped up to support the coffee price.</p>
</text>
